\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Baud Rate\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl2 \v Baud Rate}
{\xe \v Baud Rate}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAVWL}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAVWL}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Determine the baud rate used in the system.\par
 {\i {\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {\tc\tcl4 Syntax: } \par}
} \par
{\i }  {\b  baud_rate VALUE} \par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b VALUE:}  Any integer value from 110 to 256000 bits per second, including 110, 300, 600, 1200, 2400, 4800, 9600, 14400, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200, 128000, and 256000.\par}
\par
{\i {\b  Example: }  }  \par
 baud_rate 115200; \~\~\~  rem change the baud rate to 115200 bit/sec.\par
 \par
}}
\par \pard\plain 
\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
CAN Get\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl2 \v CAN Get}
{\xe \v CAN Get}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAVWM}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAVWM}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This instruction reads data from a CAN device. You might need to put the instruction in a loop to make sure that data is read correctly from the CAN device.\par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
The returned result is 1 when the data is received successfully.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
The returned result is 0 when the data is not received successfully.\par
 {\i {\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {\tc\tcl4 Syntax: } \par}
} \par}
\par
{\i }  {\b  can_get PinName1, PinName2, FREQ, CANID, VARIABLE;} \par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b PinName1:}  CANRD pin name\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b PinName2:}  CANTD pin name\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b FREQ \~\~\~\~\~ :}  CAN Bus frequency\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b CANID \~\~\~\~ :}  CAN ID. This represents the CAN device ID\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b VARIABLE_NAME:}  A Variable name is required. The results will be saved in this variable (might be an array of int).\par}
\par
{\i {\b  Example:}  }  \par
 while(1)\par
 \~\{\par
 \~can_get pb_8, pb_9, 100000,0x10,result;\par
 \~if (result!=0)\{\par
 \~\~ print result;\par
 \~ \}\par
 \~ delay 100,msec;\par
 \} \par
}}
