\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
cat help : It displays the help on the screen\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
cat <filename> : It displays the contents of the text file on the screen\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
cat -c <filename> <Script_commands> : Creates a new file and puts the <text> inside the file. <Script_commands> is optional.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
cat -a <filename1> <filename2> <filename3> : \par
 This command creates a new file named <filename1>, combines the text from <filename2> and <filename3>, and puts it in the new file.\par
}
\par
{\b Note:} \par
 An SD-card module must be connected to the Nucleo board through SPI, with an SD card inserted. The card must be mounted before using this instruction. \par
}}
