\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Delay\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl2 \v Delay}
{\xe \v Delay}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAVWV}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAVWV}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Generic wait function. It provides a simple NOP-type delay or wait capability. \par
 {\i {\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {\tc\tcl4 Syntax: } \par}
} \par
{\i }  {\b  delay VALUE,TYPE} \par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b VALUE:}  Any Integer number representing the delay\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b TYPE:}  Three types are available as follows:{
\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Sec:\~\~ The delay will be in seconds.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
mSec: The delay will be in milliseconds.\par
\pard\plain \s121\fi-360\li720\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls2\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
uSec: The delay will be in microseconds.\par
}
}
\par
{\i {\b  Example: }  }  \par
 put PA_1, 1; \~\~\~  rem put HIGH at the PA_1.\par
 delay 500,usec ; \~\~\~  rem 500 microseconds delay between the first and second instruction.\par
 put PA_1,0; \~\~\~  rem put LOW at the PA_1.\par
 \par
}}
