\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
I2C Get\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl2 \v I2C Get}
{\xe \v I2C Get}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAVXH}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAVXH}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This instruction reads data from an I2C device (master or slave). The instruction uses the standard I2C_SCL and I2C_SDA definitions.\par
 {\i {\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {\tc\tcl4 Syntax: } \par}
} \par
{\i }  {\b  i2c_get MASTER/SLAVE, address, VARIABLE_receive_data, lengthOfData;} \par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b MASTER/SLAVE:}  \~\~\~0= Master , 1=Slave\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b ADDRESS:} \~\~\~\~\~ \~\~\~\~\~\~ Address of the MASTER/SLAVE\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b VARIABLE_NAME:}  You must provide the instruction a variable name. The results will be saved in that variable (might be an array of char).\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b lengthOfData:}  \~\~\~\~\~\~\~Length of the message or data\par
}
\par
{\i {\b  Example:}  }  \par
 myvalue =\{245,133\}; i2c_send 1, 1222, myvalue,2; \~\~\~  rem read from the slave 2 bytes\par
 \par
}}
