\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Use if to specify a block of code to be executed, if a specified condition is true\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
Use else to specify a block of code to be executed, if the same condition is false {\i {\b  \par
 Example: }  }  \par
 get PA_4, myvar; \~\~\~  rem read GPIO \par
 if(myvar==0) \{\par
 \~ rem if the GPIO is zero\par
 \~print " Result was Zero\\n"\}; else \{ \~ rem if the GPIO is one\par
