\pard\plain \s2\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\kerning28\cgrid 
Put (Digital Out)\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl2 \v Put (Digital Out)}
{\xe \v Put (Digital Out)}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAVXQ}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAVXQ}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Send data to a digital pin or a digital bus. The internal definition of these GPIO is DigitalInOut and configured as output.\par
 Before using a bus you need to create it using create_reg instruction. {\i {\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {\tc\tcl4 Syntax: } \par}
} \par
{\i }  {\b  put GPIO_NAME/BUS_name, VARIABLE_NAME/NUMBER} \par
{
\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b GPIO_NAME:}  Any digital GPIO\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b BUS_name:}  A combination of multiple digital GPIOs, from 2 to 16 pins. You can combine any GPIO in the bus, but you must create it using the create_reg instruction before using this name.\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b VARIABLE_NAME:}  variable name that keeps the data\par
\pard\plain \s120\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlbody\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pndec }\ls1\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\b NUMBER:}  An integer number.\par}
\par
{\i {\b  Example:}  }  \par
 myvalue=0xff;\par
 put PA_4, myvalue; \~\~\~  rem read the value from PA_4 \par
 Or:\par
 create_reg myreg , PA_3,PA_2,PA_10_PB3; \~\~\~  rem create register \par
 put myreg, myvalue; \~\~\~  rem read the Register  \par
 \par
}}
