\par \pard\plain 
\pard\plain \s1\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs36\kerning36\cgrid 
Tutorial and Examples\par \pard\plain 
{\tc\tcl1 \v Tutorial and Examples}
{\xe \v Tutorial and Examples}
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAVYI}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAVYI}
{
\pard\plain \s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid {\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
{\pard\plain \s3\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\cgrid {\tc\tcl3 Introduction:} \par}
Writing a script program for this system is straightforward. Instruction sets can be found in the documentation. Examples show how to use each instruction.\par
Variables in this system are global, and only 32 are allowed. Inside functions, variables are local. To access a global variable from a function, pass it as an argument to the function.\par
Each instruction ends with a new line, a semicolon, or the end of the file. Commas separate arguments. A semicolon is not required at the end of a line if the line ends with a new line.\par
It is possible to write several instructions in one line separated by a semicolon.\par
Variables define themselves based on the assigned values: floating-point, integer, or string. If you no longer need a variable, it is good practice to delete it.\par
GPIOs are also saved in global variables. You can change the functionality of a GPIO without problems. You can create registers that hold multiple GPIOs, but a register cannot be used with analog input or output. You can also delete registers when you no longer need them.\par
SPI can be used to connect to peripherals. Chip Select line is multiplexed and up to 15 more devices could be connected in parallel to the SPI channel. Channel 0 of the SPI is reserved for SD-Card port.\par
I2C Lines have pull-up resistors.\par
To stop a script program, press Ctrl+C. To stop execution using a command, for example from an ICT, send the binary number 0x03 to the NUCLEO through the Tera Term serial terminal. This stops execution immediately.\par
\~Two serial ports are used in the system. One is for general communication and data exchange between the system and the outside world. The other is for debug log messages.\par
Debug com port will deliver no debug information if enable_debug command is not used in the beginning of the script file. It doesn't mean that enable_debug must be in the beginning of the script program. You can have it anywhere inside the script program. for ex. you can enable the debug messages for only a portion of the program.\par
{\b  Note:} \par
